Vampires aren't terribly dangerous in your case. First, they respect
the E-word. Second, if things get dicey, zap one of your wands at him.
If it's teleportation, he's out of your face for a while, and if it's
cancellation, he can't level-drain you anymore. If you want to melee
him, which will probably work OK, your dagger does 1d5+3+strength bonus
+skill bonus per hit, meaning it will probably out-damage a +0 long
sword on average, especially if you're skilled/expert with the dagger
and only basic with the sword. Mojo if you get it will destroy
vampires pretty quickly, but the dagger's not half bad.

All in all, I'd zap a mystery wand first. If it's cancellation, then
step back and dagger-chuck or just melee him to death, using your
teleport scroll if trouble pops up. If it's teleportation, then do the
same once he comes back, but note that level-drain is still a risk
(but much less of one with a cloak or a mithril-coat). Of course, if
the wands *are* teleportation, then you have lots of escape options.


